  "lineage": "Late-twelfth-and-thirteenth-century European art-music style centered on the Notre Dame Cathedral school of Paris under Léonin (Leoninus, fl. 1150s-1180s) and Pérotin (Perotinus, fl. 1190s-1220s). Codified rhythmic-modal notation, organum (two-, three-, and four-voice polyphony built on plainchant tenors), and clausula and motet forms. Compiled in the Magnus Liber Organi attributed to Léonin and revised by Pérotin. Distinguished from preceding plainchant by ars antiqua's systematic polyphonic-organization.",
